Package: juxtaposed
Type: Package
Title: The Juxtaposition Index J for Spatial Omics
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Junho", "Song", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "maintainer.email@to-be-confirmed.org"),
    person("Dongjoo", "Lee", role = "aut"),
    person("Jaesung", "Yoo", role = "aut"),
    person("Kwangsoo", "Kim", role = "aut"))
Description: Computes the juxtaposition index J, a bounded gradient-domain
    bivariate statistic that measures whether two features change in opposite
    or concordant directions across the same edges of a spatial graph, together
    with a regional edge-sum concordance score, Lee's L, bivariate Moran's I, Pearson correlation and codispersion on
    the same graph. Provides an exact spectral sign-flip (Moran spectral
    randomization) null with closed-form variances, which gives calibrated
    p-values for all feature pairs without permutations.
